{"When refresh_token is absent from response, it is set to literal string 'refresh_token' - downstream code may silently use this placeholder in API calls - should use null or omit field and ensure callers handle missing refresh token explicitly": 0.9247087240219116, "parseRefreshTokenResponse returns Zod SafeParseReturnType object with .success and .data properties, not parsed credential data - storing this corrupts credential as { success: true, data: {...} } instead of actual token data - need to extract .data from result": 0.9502648115158081, "When APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED and CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT are set, refreshOAuthTokens returns raw fetch Response object - accessing res?.data returns undefined, causing TypeError when accessing token.access_token - sync-endpoint response needs to be parsed with await res.json()": 0.9837660789489746, "schema.parse() throws ZodError on invalid input resulting in unhandled 500 response - should use safeParse and return 400 with validation errors": 0.6195719838142395, "If CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET is not set, undefined !== undefined evaluates to false, allowing unauthenticated access - endpoint should explicitly reject requests when secret is not configured": 0.3843521177768707, "If CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY is not set, symmetricDecrypt is called with empty string as key, producing garbage output or cryptographic error - should fail explicitly when key is missing": 0.3627546429634094}